    "source_note": "Only rustfmt line wrapping differs between the frozen benchmark sources and their checked-in counterparts. The frozen scalar implementation file exactly matches c2d147c.",
    "semantic_checks": "Every new polynomial evaluation constructs its value and requests a certified interval at precision -128. Each iteration asserts overlap with an independently constructed monomial-sum reference at -160. All fixed iteration/certificate counts and all existing root, ordering, reconstruction and image checksums are preserved.",
    "load_control": "An initial five-pair batch overlapped heavy builds and received only 58-97 percent CPU across drivers; it is retained as diagnostic data, not the headline comparison. Before the quieter repeated batch, CPU 7 was 93.07 percent idle and sibling CPU 15 was 95 percent idle. Every quieter timed process received 96-97 percent CPU. The host was not exclusive.",
    "interpretation": "The tested symbolic, nested-root and long-polynomial lanes improve materially; rational evaluation and the direct quadratic/cubic controls are effectively flat. Several parameter workloads improve while some short lanes are slightly slower, including a 57-to-63 ns rational-image lane. No blanket speedup or full competitive-performance claim is made.",
